 I watched it on television, from Toronto. The streets I'd walked to job interviews were full of smoke, and the economic order that had chosen Seattle as its showroom the season I arrived was being shouted down in front of its own display windows. It was Polanyi's double movement, staged in my old city: a market that had tried to disembed itself from society, and a society pushing back. It also looked, at moments, uncomfortably like Chapter 5. A crowd that had gathered peacefully became something else in the gas, much as the crowd research of Chapter 5 would predict: not a mob losing its mind, but a crowd being shaped by how it was treated.
 
-The second punch took longer to land. On March 10, 2000, the NASDAQ index of technology stocks reached its peak.[^v1-c7-nasdaq] Over the next two and a half years, it lost nearly four-fifths of its value. The loop Alice had warned about, prices checked against other prices rather than against the world, had finally been forced open. Seattle felt it everywhere. HomeGrocer, an online grocery company from the Eastside, merged with its rival Webvan, and the combined company went bankrupt within a year.[^v1-c7-webvan] Amazon, the bookstore in the garage three miles from my first apartment, saw its stock fall by more than ninety percent, and was widely written off.[^v1-c7-amazonfall] It survived, which is its own lesson about the difference between a story that's overpriced and a story that's false.
+The second punch took longer to land. On March 10, 2000, the NASDAQ index of technology stocks reached its peak.[^v1-c7-nasdaq] Over the next two and a half years, it lost nearly four-fifths of its value. The financial loop above, prices increasingly sustained by expectations of further price rises, had finally been forced open. Seattle felt it everywhere. HomeGrocer, an online grocery company from the Eastside, merged with its rival Webvan, and the combined company went bankrupt within a year.[^v1-c7-webvan] Amazon, the bookstore in the garage three miles from my first apartment, saw its stock fall by more than ninety percent, and was widely written off.[^v1-c7-amazonfall] It survived, which is its own lesson about the difference between a story that's overpriced and a story that's false.
 
 The economy I'd come to Seattle to join, with an empty wallet and a Corolla for a bedroom, had paid my way out of the closet and up the shore. Then, as I left, it was challenged in its streets and broken in its markets. That pattern again: the systems never seemed to collapse while I was inside them. They waited until I'd gone, as if to show me the full outline of what had held me up.
 
